narrative:
## The Leap Year Rule

A year is a leap year (366 days, February has 29) if:
- It IS divisible by 4
- AND it is NOT divisible by 100
- UNLESS it IS divisible by 400

### Translating to Code

```xiom
fn is_leap_year(year: Int) -> Bool {
  if year % 400 == 0 {
    return true;
  }
  if year % 100 == 0 {
    return false;
  }
  if year % 4 == 0 {
    return true;
  }
  return false;
}
```

### Step-by-Step Truth Table

| Year | % 400 | % 100 | % 4 | Leap? | Why |
|------|-------|-------|-----|-------|-----|
| 2024 | !=0   | !=0   | =0  | true  | Divisible by 4, not by 100 |
| 1900 | !=0   | =0    | =0  | false | Divisible by 100 but not 400 |
| 2000 | =0    | =0    | =0  | true  | Divisible by 400 trumps all |
| 2023 | !=0   | !=0   | !=0 | false | Not divisible by 4 |

### The Order Matters

Check 400 first! If you check 100 before 400, the year 2000 would be incorrectly marked as not a leap year because 2000 % 100 == 0 would trigger the false return before reaching the 400 check.

```xiom
fn main() -> Int {
  let years = [2024, 1900, 2000, 2023];
  for y in years {
    if is_leap_year(y) {
      io.println("Leap year!");
    } else {
      io.println("Not a leap year.");
    }
  }
  return 0;
}
```

